Drop `tomli` from the bootstrap `build` and `pyproject-hooks` overrides.

Upstream poetry2nix is dormant since April 2025. Recent nixpkgs (commit
8ea6bde8, "treewide: prune pythonOlder 3.10/3.11") removed the `tomli`
function arg from pkgs/development/python-modules/{build,pyproject-hooks}
since Python 3.11+ ships `tomllib` in stdlib. poetry2nix still passes
`tomli` here, which trips `makeOverridable`'s arg validation:

  error: function 'anonymous lambda' called with unexpected argument 'tomli'

Remove until upstream fixes this (nix-community/poetry2nix).

--- a/overrides/default.nix
+++ b/overrides/default.nix
@@ -160,7 +160,7 @@
       };

       build = bootstrappingBase.build.override {
-        inherit (final) buildPythonPackage flit-core packaging pyproject-hooks tomli;
+        inherit (final) buildPythonPackage flit-core packaging pyproject-hooks;
       };

       flit-core = bootstrappingBase.flit-core.override {
@@ -176,7 +176,7 @@
       };

       pyproject-hooks = bootstrappingBase.pyproject-hooks.override {
-        inherit (final) buildPythonPackage flit-core tomli;
+        inherit (final) buildPythonPackage flit-core;
       };

